Question	Answer
What is memory allocation?	Assigning available memory to processes.
What is First Fit?	Allocating the first suitable memory block.
What is Best Fit?	Allocating the smallest suitable memory block.
What is Worst Fit?	Allocating the largest suitable memory block.
Which algorithm generally searches fewer blocks?	First Fit.
What is fragmentation?	Memory becoming wasted or difficult to utilize.
What is internal fragmentation?	Unused space inside an allocated partition.
What is external fragmentation?	Free memory scattered across separate holes.
What is compaction?	Combining scattered free memory into a larger contiguous region by relocating allocated regions.
What happens if no suitable block exists?	The process remains unallocated.
Which algorithm performs best for the given input?	Best Fit.
What is the worst-case time complexity of these programs?	O(n × m), where n is processes and m is blocks.
